<title>USA: Santa Fe Energy Q1 revs, net, share rise.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe Energy Q1 revs, net, share rise.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions of dollars, except as noted)</p>
<p>   Three Months Ended March 31,		    1997   1996(1)</p>
<p>REVENUES</p>
<p>  Sales of crude oil and liquids produced	  127.3   98.6</p>
<p>  Sales of natural gas produced			 36.7   24.9</p>
<p>  Sales of crude oil purchased			   9.6    0.0</p>
<p>  Other							  0.3    0.2</p>
<p>		  Total Revenues			   173.9  123.7</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES</p>
<p>  Production and operating				52.2   44.0</p>
<p>  Cost of crude oil purchased			   10.7    0.0</p>
<p>  Exploration, including dry hole costs		9.3    5.6</p>
<p>  Depl., depr. and amort.				 33.6   32.3</p>
<p>  General and administrative			     7.1    6.0</p>
<p>  Taxes (other than income)				7.5    6.1</p>
<p>  Loss (gain) on disposition of assets	     (2.3)    0.2</p>
<p>     Total Costs and Expenses			  118.1   94.2</p>
<p> Income from Operations				   55.8   29.5</p>
<p>  Interest income					    0.9    0.5</p>
<p>  Interest expense					 (7.7)  (9.6)</p>
<p>  Interest capitalized				     1.6    1.3</p>
<p>  Other income					     (0.1)  (0.3)</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes and Minority Interest	  50.5   21.4</p>
<p>Income taxes</p>
<p>     Current						 (4.5)  (2.1)</p>
<p>     Deferred					     (15.4)  (6.7)</p>
<p> Income Before Minority Interest			30.6   12.6</p>
<p>  Minority interest in Monterey Resources, Inc.  (2.7)    0.0</p>
<p> Net Income						   27.9   12.6</p>
<p>  Preferred dividend requirement		     (2.4)  (3.7)</p>
<p> Earnings to Common Shares				25.5    8.9</p>
<p> Earnings per Share (in dollars)			0.28   0.10</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding (in millions)	   91.2   90.4</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) Certain amounts restated to conform to 1997 presentation. Reported earnings include SFR's ownership in its subsidiary Monterey Resources, which is engaged primarily in the production of heavy crude oil in California. SFR owns 83 percent of Monterey's common stock and intends to distribute those shares to SFR's common shareholders in Q3 1997.</p>
<p>On a pro forma basis, the &quot;new&quot; Santa Fe, excluding Monterey, had Q1 1997 earnings of $14.6 million, or $0.16 per share, compared with break-even results for Q1 1996.</p>
<p>The &quot;new&quot; Santa Fe had pro forma revenues of $89.0 million for Q1 1997, up from $64.1 million in corresponding period last year, due to increased production and improved oil and gas prices.</p>
</text>
